I have found an apparent bug involving bags and ghost piles. Ordinarily, if
you are carrying a named weapon, and you encounter the same sort of weapon
on a ghost pile, the ghost weapon will lose its name, but your weapon is
unaffected. HOWEVER, if you put, say, your +3 Orcrist in a bag of holding,
and then come across a barbarian ghost who had Orcrist, you will find that
not only does the 2-h sword on the ghost pile have no name, but also that
when you remove your Orcrist from your bag, *it* no longer has a name.
Furthermore, the flag for the existence of Orcrist remains set, so you
can't just name your sword Orcrist again.

As far as I can tell, this bug is not just limited to artifacts. I had a game
where I had named my athame, and then put it in a bag. Then I found a wizard
ghost with an athame. When I removed my athame from the bag, it had lost its
name.

The moral of this story: Don't put artifacts in bags!

By the way, I discovered this bug during my most recent game of nethack, which
was my first win. (1.1 M points -- just playing to finish.)

I also encountered another weird bug in this game -- a troll with over 7000 HP!
I was cleaning out this treasure zoo, killed a troll in it, and started
eating him. I was interrupted by another monster, and the troll came back to 
life. I killed him again, was interrupted again, and again he came back to
life. But in his third incarnation, no matter how much I hit him, he didn't
die. So I checked him with my stethoscope, and discovered, to my horror,
that his hit points registered 7200(48)! I zapped him with my wand of
polymorph (I had no death wand) and he turned into an ettin zombie with
6900 HP. Somehow, I eventually killed him.

The up side of this story is that when I gathered the gold from the zoo, it
totalled over 40,000 GP. I suppose this extraordinary amount of treasure was
linked to the troll's HP. (The fact that there was a temple on the next level
which allowed me to trade in all that gold for AC contributed significantly
to my winning the game.)

Jonathan


